      "id": "jvntr2t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was aimed at achieving growth, modernization, self-reliance, and social justice.",
        "The Planning Commission was set up in March 1950 as an extra-constitutional and non-statutory body headed by the Prime Minister.",
        "India completed 12 Five-Year Plans between 1951 and 2017 before transitioning to a new planning framework.",
        "NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India) replaced the Planning Commission on January 1, 2015.",
        "NITI Aayog serves as a think tank promoting cooperative federalism and a bottom-up approach to national development."
      ],
      "id": "b6pajge"
    },
