    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The First Five-Year Plan (1951-56) was based on the Harrod-Domar Model and focused on agricultural development.",
        "The Second Five-Year Plan (1956-61) was based on the Mahalanobis Model, prioritizing rapid industrialization and heavy industries.",
        "Unlike the Planning Commission, NITI Aayog does not possess the power to allocate financial funds to states.",
        "The Governing Council of NITI Aayog comprises Chief Ministers of all States and Lt. Governors of Union Territories."
      ],
      "id": "wui1dlx"
